class:: BlipPM
summary:: Finite Blip kernel with sample-accurate shared phase modulation
categories:: UGens>Generators>Deterministic
related:: Guides/BlipExtensions, Classes/BlipAD, Classes/BlipDecay, Classes/BlipDiff, Classes/BlipDisp, Classes/BlipFB, Classes/BlipFrac, Classes/BlipInt, Classes/BlipKernel, Classes/BlipPeak, Classes/BlipPower, Classes/BlipSeries, Classes/BlipWidth

description::

BlipPM evaluates the finite rectangular kernel at the internal carrier phase
plus code::phase::. A shared displacement acts code::k:: times as strongly on
harmonic code::k::, exactly as in the equivalent additive bank.

The carrier accumulator never absorbs the modulation input. Large finite
phase values are wrapped before evaluation, and deliberate input
discontinuities can click without corrupting carrier state. The carrier
harmonics are Nyquist-limited, but audio-rate phase modulation creates
sidebands outside that set and is not strictly bandlimited.

The closest vanilla comparison is link::Classes/PMOsc::. BlipPM modulates one
finite harmonic kernel rather than one sinusoidal carrier, and exposes the
phase displacement directly in radians.

classmethods::

method:: ar

argument:: freq
Carrier frequency in Hz. Audio or control rate; signed values are valid.

argument:: numharm
Carrier harmonic count, sampled once per block and clipped to code::1..2048::
before Nyquist limiting.

argument:: phase
Unrestricted finite phase displacement in radians at audio or control rate.

argument:: mul
Post-processing multiplier.

argument:: add
Post-processing offset.

examples::

code::
(
{ BlipPM.ar(100, 40, SinOsc.ar(3) * 0.2, 0.1) }.play;
)
::

code::
(
{ BlipPM.ar(80, 60, SinOsc.ar(120) * 0.05, 0.1) }.play;
)
::

code::
// Modulating all parameters for a dynamic sound
(
{ BlipPM.ar(MouseX.kr(50, 500, 'exponential'), MouseY.kr(1, 100), SinOsc.ar(100) * MouseY.kr(0, 2pi)) ! 2 * 0.1 }.play;
)
::
